#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:17
msgid "Abstract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:19
msgid ""
"Add a new C API to import and export Python integers, :class:`int` objects: "
"especially :c:func:`PyLongWriter_Create()` and :c:func:`PyLong_Export()` "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:24
msgid "Rationale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:26
msgid ""
"Projects such as `gmpy2 <https://github.com/aleaxit/gmpy>`_, `SAGE <https://"
"www.sagemath.org/>`_ and `Python-FLINT <https://github.com/flintlib/python-"
"flint>`_ access directly Python \"internals\" (the :c:type:`PyLongObject` "
"structure) or use an inefficient temporary format (hex strings for Python-"
"FLINT) to import and export Python :class:`int` objects.  The Python :class:"
"`int` implementation changed in Python 3.12 to add a tag and \"compact "
"values\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:34
msgid ""
"In the 3.13 alpha 1 release, the private undocumented :c:func:`!"
"_PyLong_New()` function had been removed, but it is being used by these "
"projects to import Python integers. The private function has been restored "
"in 3.13 alpha 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:39
msgid ""
"A public efficient abstraction is needed to interface Python with these "
"projects without exposing implementation details. It would allow Python to "
"change its internals without breaking these projects.  For example, "
"implementation for gmpy2 was changed recently for CPython 3.9 and for "
"CPython 3.12."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:47
msgid "Specification"
msgstr ""

