msgid ""
"Data needed by `GMP <https://gmplib.org/>`_-like `import <https://gmplib.org/"
"manual/Integer-Import-and-Export#index-mpz_005fimport>`_-`export <https://"
"gmplib.org/manual/Integer-Import-and-Export#index-mpz_005fexport>`_ "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:59
msgid ""
"Layout of an array of \"digits\" (\"limbs\" in the GMP terminology), used to "
"represent absolute value for arbitrary precision integers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:62
msgid ""
"Use :c:func:`PyLong_GetNativeLayout` to get the native layout of Python :"
"class:`int` objects, used internally for integers with \"big enough\" "
"absolute value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:66
msgid ""
"See also :data:`sys.int_info` which exposes similar information to Python."
msgstr ""

