#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:402
msgid "Rejected Ideas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:405
msgid "Support arbitrary layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:407
msgid ""
"It would be convenient to support arbitrary layout to import-export Python "
"integers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:410
msgid ""
"For example, it was proposed to add a *layout* parameter to :c:func:"
"`PyLongWriter_Create()` and a *layout* member to the :c:struct:"
"`PyLongExport` structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:414
msgid ""
"The problem is that it's more complex to implement and not really needed. "
"What's strictly needed is only an API to import-export using the Python "
"\"native\" layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:418
msgid ""
"If later there are use cases for arbitrary layouts, new APIs can be added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:423
msgid "Don't add :c:func:`PyLong_GetNativeLayout` function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:425
msgid ""
"Currently, most required information for :class:`int` import/export is "
"already available via :c:func:`PyLong_GetInfo()` (and :data:`sys."
"int_info`).  We also can add more (like order of digits), this interface "
"doesn't poses any constraints on future evolution of the :c:type:"
"`PyLongObject`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:430
msgid ""
"The problem is that the :c:func:`PyLong_GetInfo()` returns a Python object, :"
"term:`named tuple`, not a convenient C structure and that might distract "
"people from using it in favor e.g. of current semi-private macros like :c:"
"macro:`!PyLong_SHIFT` and :c:macro:`!PyLong_BASE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:437
msgid "Provide mpz_import/export-like API instead"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:439
msgid ""
"The other approach to import/export data from :class:`int` objects might be "
"following: expect, that C extensions provide contiguous buffers that CPython "
"then exports (or imports) the *absolute* value of an integer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:443
msgid "API example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:455
msgid ""
"This might work for the GMP, as this it has :c:func:`!mpz_limbs_read()` and :"
"c:func:`!mpz_limbs_write()` functions, that can provide required \"buffers\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0757.rst:458
msgid ""
"The major drawback of this approach is that it's much more complex on the "
"CPython side (i.e. actual conversion between different layouts)."
msgstr ""

